### Describe the bug

Two one-element Arrow lists can both represent `[NULL]` when one contains a null dictionary key and the other contains a key pointing to a null dictionary value. `GROUPS BETWEEN CURRENT ROW AND CURRENT ROW` counts one row in each group. `rank()` and `dense_rank()` also split the peers when the planner chooses `BoundedWindowAggExec`.

### To reproduce

Register this two-row batch in a Rust `SessionContext`.

```rust
use std::sync::Arc;
use datafusion::arrow::{
    array::{ArrayRef, DictionaryArray, Int8Array, Int32Array, ListArray, RecordBatch},
    buffer::OffsetBuffer,
    datatypes::{Field, Int8Type},
};
use datafusion::prelude::{SessionConfig, SessionContext};

let children: ArrayRef = Arc::new(DictionaryArray::<Int8Type>::try_new(
    Int8Array::from(vec![None, Some(0)]),
    Arc::new(Int32Array::from(vec![None])),
)?);
let key: ArrayRef = Arc::new(ListArray::new(
    Arc::new(Field::new("item", children.data_type().clone(), true)),
    OffsetBuffer::from_lengths([1, 1]), children, None,
));
let ctx = SessionContext::new_with_config(SessionConfig::new().with_target_partitions(1));
ctx.register_batch("t", RecordBatch::try_from_iter([("k", key)])?)?;
```

Run these queries in that context.

```sql
SELECT count(*) OVER (ORDER BY k GROUPS BETWEEN CURRENT ROW AND CURRENT ROW) FROM t;

SELECT rank() OVER w, dense_rank() OVER w FROM t WINDOW w AS (ORDER BY k);

SELECT rank() OVER w, dense_rank() OVER w, percent_rank() OVER w
FROM t WINDOW w AS (ORDER BY k);
```

| Query | Physical operator observed | Output for the two rows | Expected |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| GROUPS count | `BoundedWindowAggExec` (Sorted) | `1, 1` | `2, 2` |
| Rank and dense rank | `BoundedWindowAggExec` (Sorted) | `1, 2` for each function | `1, 1` for each function |
| Rank and dense rank alongside percent rank | `WindowAggExec` | `1, 1` for each rank function and `0.0, 0.0` for percent rank | Same |

Reproduced at `99100274dd` during review of #26067. GROUPS frame boundaries and bounded rank compare extracted `ScalarValue`s. Batch rank uses Arrow partition boundaries, which group the two rows together. [GROUPS boundaries](https://github.com/apache/datafusion/blob/99100274dd139574854e40393474caac5c97e16b/datafusion/expr/src/window_state.rs#L710-L739) · [bounded rank](https://github.com/apache/datafusion/blob/99100274dd139574854e40393474caac5c97e16b/datafusion/functions-window/src/rank.rs#L276-L308) · [batch rank](https://github.com/apache/datafusion/blob/99100274dd139574854e40393474caac5c97e16b/datafusion/physical-expr/src/window/standard.rs#L144-L147)
